.TH JANUSGATE-NETD 8 "August 2026" "JanusGate 0.1.3" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
janusgate-netd \- run the privileged JanusGate network helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B janusgate-netd
.br
.B janusgate-netd --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B janusgate-netd
owns the narrow privileged boundary used to validate and apply JanusGate
bridge, native packet-selection, packet-queue, reboot, and power-off
operations.
It accepts only bounded versioned requests from the configured
.B janusgate
service identity over a Unix
.B SOCK_SEQPACKET
socket.
.PP
Network changes are transactional.
An applied change must be confirmed within 120 seconds or the captured bridge
and packet-selection state is restored.
Lifecycle and failure records use the structured JanusGate logging format.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --version
Display build version information and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/janusgate/netd.sock
Authenticated network-helper socket on Linux.
.TP
.I /var/run/janusgate/netd.sock
Authenticated network-helper socket on OpenBSD.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The helper stopped cleanly or version information was displayed.
.TP
.B 1
Required privilege, identity resolution, or runtime processing failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH SECURITY
This helper must run as root under the supplied init definition.
Do not expose its socket outside the local machine or grant access to
identities other than the dedicated policy service.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR janusgatectl (1),
.BR janusgated (8),
.BR janusgate-web (8)
